The '''W213 Mercedes-Benz E-Class''' is the fifth generation of the [[Mercedes-Benz E-Class]], sold from 2016 as a 2017 model. It succeeded the [[Mercedes-Benz E-Class (W212)|W212/S212 E-Class]] models. The [[coupe]]/[[convertible]] models share the same platform as the [[Sedan (automobile)|sedan]]/wagon, in contrast to the previous generation. The high-performance [[Mercedes-AMG]] E 63 and E 63 S versions of the W213 have been available as well from 2016 (as a 2017 model), and these are the only versions with [[V8 engine]]s.

Since the mid-1990s, the Mercedes-Benz E-Class has been equipped with quad headlights and a differentiated design compared to the [[Mercedes-Benz C-Class|C-Class]] and [[Mercedes-Benz S-Class|S-Class]]. With the 2017 model, Mercedes decided to take a more streamlined direction, first seen with the [[Mercedes-Benz E-Class (W212)#W212 facelift (2013–2016)|2014 E-Class]] [[Facelift (automotive)|mid-generational refresh]] and then going in an entirely new direction with the all-new 2017 model.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.autospies.com/news/SPIED-BEST-Look-Yet-At-The-All-New-Mercedes-Benz-E-Class-Get-A-Peek-At-Its-All-New-Mug-86516/|title=SPIED: BEST Look Yet At The All-New Mercedes-Benz E-Class — Get A Peek At Its All-New Mug|access-date=3 November 2015|archive-date=7 December 2015|archive-url=https://archive.today/20151207123026/http://www.autospies.com/news/SPIED-BEST-Look-Yet-At-The-All-New-Mercedes-Benz-E-Class-Get-A-Peek-At-Its-All-New-Mug-86516/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Launched in spring 2016 following a world debut at the [[North American International Auto Show#2016|2016 North American International Auto Show]] in January, the 2017 E-Class was the most technologically advanced car Mercedes had ever produced at the time.<ref name="2016eclassautocar"/> This generation of the Mercedes E-Class has won many plaudits from automotive publications, including the 2021 [[Motor Trend Car of the Year]], the first time Mercedes-Benz has ever won this award.<ref>{{cite web|date=16 November 2020|title=The Mercedes-Benz E-Class Is the 2021 MotorTrend Car of the Year|url=https://www.motortrend.com/cars/mercedes-benz/e-class/2021/mercedes-benz-e-class-2021-car-of-the-year/|access-date=20 November 2020|website=MotorTrend|language=en}}</ref>

== Development and launch ==
The whole development process stretched over 48 months. In that time, Mercedes-Benz produced 1,200 prototypes and drove a combined 12 million kilometres in some of the world's toughest conditions, from sub-zero temperatures in the snow through to the world's hottest deserts.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.carscoops.com/2015/12/mercedes-benz-has-tested-upcoming-e.html |title=Mercedes-Benz Has Tested The Upcoming E-Class For 12 Million Kilometers |publisher=Carscoops |date= 27 December 2015 |accessdate=12 August 2022}}</ref> In testing the car, Mercedes-Benz also had its prototypes conduct over 10,000 autonomous braking procedures and 5,000 automated lane changes as part of the Distronic suite of semi-autonomous driving features.<ref>{{cite web| url = http://www.motortrend.com/news/watch-the-2017-mercedes-benz-e-class-undergo-extreme-testing/| title = Watch the 2017 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Undergo Extreme Testing| date = 26 December 2015}}</ref> Moreover, it took 1,200 engineers to make the fifth-generation E-Class.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.benzinsider.com/2015/12/another-video-teaser-of-the-mercedes-benz-e-class-is-out/ |title=Another Video Teaser of the Mercedes-Benz E-Class is Out |date=27 December 2015 |access-date=28 December 2015 |archive-date=4 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304090751/http://www.benzinsider.com/2015/12/another-video-teaser-of-the-mercedes-benz-e-class-is-out/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The W213 E-Class was unveiled at the [[North American International Auto Show#2016|2016 North American International Auto Show]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.nydailynews.com/autos/auto-shows/detroit-auto-show-2017-mercedes-benz-e-class-article-1.2491787 |title=Detroit Auto Show: 2017 Mercedes-Benz E-Class is all-new, but entirely familiar |website=[[Daily News (New York)|Daily News]]|location=New York |date=10 January 2016 |access-date=11 January 2016 |archive-date=12 January 2016 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20160112081628/http://www.nydailynews.com/autos/auto-shows/detroit-auto-show-2017-mercedes-benz-e-class-article-1.2491787 |url-status=live }}</ref> The 2017 E-Class has a design similar to that of the larger [[Mercedes-Benz S-Class (W222)|W222 S-Class]] and the smaller [[Mercedes-Benz C-Class (W205)|W205 C-Class]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.autoevolution.com/news/2016-mercedes-e-class-w213-first-interior-spy-photos-s-class-inspiration-89573.html#|title=2016 Mercedes E-Class (W213) First Interior Spy Photos: S-CLass Inspiration|author=Mihnea Radu|work=autoevolution|date=3 December 2014}}</ref> While its predecessor had a tighter surface and harder edges, the 2017 model is curvier and more flowing.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://indianautosblog.com/2015/05/2016-mercedes-e-class-naias-2016-178443|title=2016 Mercedes E Class to world debut at NAIAS 2016|work=indianautosblog.com|date=11 May 2015}}</ref> An official design sketch was released in late December 2015, which confirmed that the new E-Class mirrors the styling of the C-Class and S-Class.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://blog.caranddriver.com/sketchy-mercedes-benz-teases-the-new-2017-e-class/ |title=Sketchy: Mercedes-Benz Teases the New 2017 E-class |date=31 December 2015 |access-date=2 January 2016 |archive-date=5 January 2016 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20160105102843/http://blog.caranddriver.com/sketchy-mercedes-benz-teases-the-new-2017-e-class/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Official photos of the 2017 E-Class were leaked on the internet on 4 January 2016 ahead of its unveiling.<ref>{{cite web| url = http://www.motorauthority.com/news/1101673_2017-mercedes-benz-e-class-leaked| title = 2017 Mercedes-Benz E-Class Leaked| date = 4 January 2016}}</ref>

The W213 was first released in the saloon configuration, which went on sale in the summer of 2016. The Estate, offering a similar 695-litre luggage capacity to its predecessor, went to sale towards the end of 2016.<ref name="2016eclassautocar"/> A two-door Coupe arrived in 2017, before the Convertible completes the line-up towards the end of 2017.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.autoexpress.co.uk/mercedes/e-class/89072/mercedes-e-class-2016-exclusive-pics-and-latest-details|title=Mercedes E-Class 2016: full details and latest images|work=Auto Express|access-date=20 October 2015|archive-date=7 December 2015|archive-url=https://archive.today/20151207131859/http://www.autoexpress.co.uk/mercedes/e-class/89072/mercedes-e-class-2016-exclusive-pics-and-latest-details|url-status=live}}</ref> The W213 E-Class was deemed one of ''Car and Driver's'' "10 Best vehicles" in 2019.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.caranddriver.com/features/g26426806/10best-cars-winners-2019-flipbook/|title=2019 10 Best Cars|last=Car and Driver|date=22 February 2019|magazine=[[Car and Driver]]|language=en-US|access-date=28 September 2019}}</ref>

