Stylistically, the 2017 E-Class followed the latest [[Mercedes-Benz C-Class (W205)|C-Class]], the [[Mercedes-Benz GLA-Class|GLA]], and the [[Mercedes-Benz S-Class (C217)|S-Class coupé]]. Its front end features Mercedes’ familiar bullet-shaped headlights and an upright grille, while its rear end gets a pair of LED taillights, with similarities to the [[Mercedes-Benz E-Class (W212)|2014 E-Class models]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.gtspirit.com/2015/11/02/next-gen-mercedes-benz-e-class-spied-almost-undisguised/|title = Next-Gen Mercedes-Benz E-Class Spied Almost Undisguised| date=2 November 2015 }}</ref> that extend into the quarter panels.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.digitaltrends.com/cars/2017-mercedes-benz-e-class-news-specs-rumors/|title=2017 Mercedes-Benz E-Class - News, Specs, Rumors - Digital Trends|date=6 June 2015|work=Digital Trends}}</ref> As on other recent models, the 2017 E-Class features two distinct front-end treatments: a traditional chrome grille and a more sporting blade grille.<ref name="2016eclassautocar"/> The aerodynamic efficiency have been refined as the drag coefficient improved from 0.25 in the previous model to a class-leading 0.23.<ref name="E-Class revealed"/>

