For the 2021 facelift, the E 450's M276 Biturbo V6 was dropped for the new [[Mercedes-Benz M256 engine|M256]] 3.0L inline-6 turbo with EQ Boost. Power outputs are unchanged at {{Convert|362|PS|hp kW|abbr=on}} and {{Convert|500|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}}.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2019 Mercedes-Benz E-Class adds 362-horsepower E450 model |url=https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1116902_2019-mercedes-benz-e-class-adds-362-horsepower-e450-model |access-date=15 May 2023 |website=motorauthority.com|date=25 May 2018 }}</ref> The E 200 and E 300 were similarly updated in 2021, from the M274 turbo inline-four to the [[Mercedes-Benz M260/M264 engine|M264]] 2.0L turbo I4 engine with EQ Boost, producing {{Convert|197|PS|kW hp|abbr=on}} and {{Convert|320|Nm|4=0|abbr=on}} in the E 200, and {{Convert|258|PS|kW hp|abbr=on}} and {{Convert|370|Nm|4=0|abbr=on}} in the E 300.

The only AMG variant of the C238/A238 E-Class Coupé and Cabriolet is the E 53 AMG 4MATIC+ produced from 2019 onwards, powered by the [[Mercedes-Benz M256 engine|M256]] 3.0L inline 6 turbo with EQ Boost engine, producing {{Convert|435|PS|hp kW|abbr=on}} and {{convert|520|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}}.<ref name=":2" />

